mode: "100644"
text: "# Hooks & Retention on TikTok\n\nWatch time, completion, and rewatches are the FYP's top signals — so the hook and the retention\ndesign are where a TikTok is won or lost. This is the craft layer.\n\n## The first second\n\nYou have ~1 second to stop the scroll, and ~3 to convince them to stay. Fire on three channels at\nonce:\n\n- **Verbal hook** — the first words out of your mouth (or the voiceover's). No preamble.\n- **On-screen text hook** — a bold text line that states the stakes/curiosity (also caught by\n  sound-off viewers).\n- **Visual hook** — motion, a striking first frame, a pattern interrupt (do something unexpected in\n  frame).\n\nPull the hook mechanism from `hook-writer`. Banned openings: \"Hey guys,\" a logo/intro card, a slow\npan, \"In this video I'm going to…\". Start *in* the action or the claim.\n\n## Hook angles that work on TikTok\n\n- **The bold claim / contrarian** — \"Your most-requested feature is the one to delete.\"\n- **The open loop** — \"I lost $40k learning this. Here's the 20-second version.\"\n- **The result / number** — \"We went from 0 to 10k users with one boring button.\"\n- **The callout** — \"If you run a SaaS, stop doing this.\"\n- **The POV / relatable** — \"POV: the feature everyone begged for, that nobody used.\"\n- **The \"wait for it\"** — promise a payoff that requires watching to the end (loop fuel).\n\nWhatever the angle, it must be **true** — no clickbait the video doesn't pay off. A betrayed hook\ntanks watch time on the *next* video too (TikTok learns).\n\n## Retention design — keep them to the end\n\n- **No intro tax.** The value starts at second 0. Cut anything before the hook.\n- **Fast pace.** Tight cuts, no dead air, no rambling. Trim every pause.\n- **Open loops.** Pose the question early, answer it late (\"the third one surprised me\").\n- **Re-hook mid-video.** A second curiosity bump around the middle for longer videos.\n- **Front-load value, but hold one payoff** for the end to pull completion.\n- **Captions/on-screen text** keep sound-off viewers in.\n\n## Design for the rewatch / loop\n\nRewatches are one of the most powerful signals, and the most underused lever:\n\n- **Seamless loop** — end the video so the last frame/line flows back into the first, so it replays\n  without a seam. The viewer watches twice before realizing.\n- **The rewatch trigger** — a detail, a fast line, or a \"did you catch…\" that rewards (and invites)\n  a second watch.\n- **Density** — pack enough that one watch isn't enough to absorb it (great for listicles/tips).\n\n## Retention killers (cut these)\n\n- A slow or branded intro.\n- Burying the point (\"so basically, what happened was, um…\").\n- Dead air / long pauses / filler.\n- A hook the video doesn't deliver.\n- Reading a script stiffly — TikTok rewards energy and a real person.\n\n## The measurable check\n\nA good TikTok script can answer: what's the **1-second hook** (all three channels)? where's the\n**open loop**? what's the **loop/rewatch trigger**? is there **any** dead air? If the hook is weak\nor the loop is missing, fix those before anything else.\n"
